From 3c98c7979c0c86876cdf5c107765604081cd84d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritesh Pandit <riteshp2001@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:00:01 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 136/140] fix(player): revise yt-dlp installation and promote
 secondary subtitles

Restore compatible yt-dlp installation handling
- Restore the pre-regression nonempty-file installation check instead of
  using Java ZIP entry inspection for the downloaded yt-dlp executable.
- Require only setup.py, the bundled Python library, and CA certificates
  during runtime preparation. Keep the legacy shell wrapper optional.
- Validate each newly downloaded candidate with the bundled libytdl.so
  launcher and --ignore-config --version before replacing the installed
  file. Bound this validation to 30 seconds and retain the previous file
  if download or validation fails.
- Preserve serialized runtime preparation and temporary-file replacement.

Expose installation failures
- Capture bounded installer/update output in yt-dlp Streaming settings
  instead of discarding it. Show the existing localized failure message
  and selectable diagnostic details when an operation fails.
- Prevent duplicate operations and reset busy/error state for retries,
  while preserving coroutine cancellation.

Subtitle selection and indicator placement
- When both tracks are selected and Primary is unchecked, clear the
  secondary slot and promote its track to Primary. Reuse subtitle-layout
  synchronization to apply the primary position.
- Keep secondary-only deselection and single-primary deselection behavior.
- Move P/S indicators to the trailing side of the subtitle row, beside the
  delete action, without changing selection callbacks.

Validation and history
- Reviewed the focused five-file patch, track-property/layout wiring,
  installer launcher contract, editor diagnostics, and git diff --check.
- Validation remains static-only: no builds, tests, installer execution,
  emulator, or device playback checks were run. The exact device-specific
  installation failure has not been reproduced; runtime verification is
  still required.
- Add this as a separate commit after 6d059791, retaining 5c5d4d91 and both
  later published commits unchanged as requested. No generated schemas,
  changelog files, or unrelated code were modified.
